    std_spec_package_shadows_file_print_summary_2026-07-17, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep-20261127: interpreter symptom (E1002 print_summary not found) was already fixed by landed Rust-side loader work (file-first redirect + rt_bdd_* bridge); verified all three doc scenarios fail-closed correctly on fresh HEAD seed. The remaining pure-Simple half: the canonical package surface std.nogc_sync_mut.spec (the __init__) was the only tier surface not re-exporting the file's summary accessors, so any consumer stopping at the package surface saw the package shadow the file. Fix: one export-use line + comment in src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/spec/__init__.spl mirroring the nogc_async_mut/gc_async_mut/gc_sync_mut shims. New spec test/01_unit/lib/std/spec/package_print_summary_surface_spec.spl 2/2 PASS (static surface contract fails pre-fix; runtime subprocess contract). Neighbours spec_summary_after_describe 1/1, pending_runtime_accounting, decorators, skip_governance, dir_prevention, result_wrapper specs PASS. Pre-existing it_block_error_accumulation_spec 2/5 failure is environment-dependent and identical with/without the change. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/lib/std/spec/package_print_summary_surface_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/lib/std/spec/spec_summary_after_describe_spec.spl"

